@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@
@@ Commands to define constants and store them in the database.

«
@@ Add a constant type "Basic = Without uncertainty, without unit" to the database.
@@ The Value is expected to have no unit.
@@ Both the Standard and Relative Uncertainty are taken to be 0.
@@ (<name> <description> <value> -- )

	@ Push uncertainties.
	0 0

	@ Create Constant object.
	5 ToList

	ConstantAddToDatabase
»
ConstantBasicDefinition Store

«
@@ Add a constant type "Exact definition" to the database.
@@ The Value is expected to have a unit.
@@ Both the Standard and Relative Uncertainty are taken to be 0.
@@ The Standard Uncertainty will get the unit of the Value.
@@ (<name> <description> <value> -- )

     	→ value
	«
		@ Push the value.
		value

		@ Push 0 StandardUncertainty with the unit of the value.
		0 value ToUnit

		@ Push 0 RelativeUncertainty.
		0

		@ Create Constant object.
		5 ToList

		ConstantAddToDatabase
	»
»
ConstantExactDefinition Store

'ConstantExactDefinition'
ConstantDefinitionConvention Store
'ConstantExactDefinition'
ConstantTheoryApproximation Store


«
@@ Add a constant type "Exact calculation" to the database.
@@ The Value is expected to have a unit.
@@ The desired unit is to be provided as a separate argument.
@@ Both the Standard and Relative Uncertainty are taken to be 0.
@@ The Value and Standard Uncertainty will get the desired unit.
@@ (<name> <description> <value> <unit> -- )

     	→ value unit
	«
		@ Push the value with the unit
		value unit Convert

		@ Push 0 StandardUncertainty with the unit.
		0 unit ToUnit

		@ Push 0 RelativeUncertainty.
		0

		@ Create Constant object.
		5 ToList

		ConstantAddToDatabase
	»
»
ConstantExactCalculation Store

'ConstantExactCalculation'
ConstantCalculationConvention Store

«
@@ Add a constant type "Measurement" to the database.
@@ The Value and the Standard Uncertainty are expected the have the same unit.
@@ From those the Relative Uncertainty is calculated and properly rounded.
@@ (<name> <description> <value> <StandardUncertainty> -- )

     	→ value sUncertainty
	«
		@ Push the value, with or without a unit
		value

		@ Push the StandardUncertainty, with or without a unit
		sUncertainty

		@ Push the RelativeUncertainty.
		sUncertainty value abs /  -2 Round

		@ Create Constant object.
		5 ToList

		ConstantAddToDatabase
	»
»
ConstantMeasurement Store


«
@@ Add a constant type "Calculated from measurement" to the database.
@@ The Value is expected to have a unit.
@@ The desired unit is to be provided as a separate argument.
@@ If TypeName unit != "unit" no conversion is done.
@@ The Standard Uncertainty is calculated and properly rounded.
@@ (<name> <description> <value> <relative uncertainty> <unit> -- )

        → value rUncertainty unit
        «
                @ Calculate the Value with the proper rounding and unit.

                @ Cast to the desired units.
                value

		If
			unit TypeName "unit" =
		Then
			unit Convert
		End

                @ Determine the rounding.
                value rUncertainty Multiply Exponent
                value Exponent
                Subtract 2 Subtract

                @ Finish the value.
                Round
                ToDecimal

                @ Calculate the StandardUncertainty with the proper rounding and unit.
                Duplicate abs  rUncertainty  Multiply

		If
			unit TypeName "unit" =
		Then
			BaseUnits
			-2 round
			unit Convert
		End

		-2 Round
                ToDecimal

                @ Push the RelativeUncertainty.
		@ Force rounding.
                rUncertainty
		-2 round

                @ Create Constant object.
                5 ToList

                ConstantAddToDatabase
        »
»
ConstantCalculationFromMeasurement Store


»
